{"definition":"A decycling set is a set \\(S\\subseteq V(G)\\) such that \\(G-S\\) is a forest, meaning it has no cycles. The decycling number is the minimum cardinality of a decycling set. This is also known as a feedback vertex set number in many graph-theory contexts.","dependencies":[],"dimension":null,"exactness":"exact","expression":{"arguments":[{"kind":"variable","name":"G","sort":{"key":"graph_theory.finite_connected_simple_graph_value","parameters":[]}}],"kind":"application","symbol":"graph_theory.decycling_number"},"hypothesis_eligible":false,"key":"graph_theory.decycling_number","name":"Decycling number","observation_key":"decycling_number","predictor_eligible":true,"provenance_references":["reference:theo-conjecture-web-fresh-graph-registry","source:theox-graph-template-normalization"],"role":"established","scalar_constraints":[],"subject":{"kind":"variable","name":"G","sort":{"key":"graph_theory.finite_connected_simple_graph_value","parameters":[]}},"target_eligible":true,"unit":null,"value_kind":"integer","value_sort":{"key":"core.integer_value","parameters":[]}}
{"definition":"For a simple graph with n(G) >= 2, there are n(G)(n(G)-1)/2 possible edges. The density of G is m(G) divided by this number, equivalently 2m(G)/(n(G)(n(G)-1)). A density of 0 means no possible edges are present, and a density of 1 means G is complete.","dependencies":[{"descriptor_key":"graph_theory.m","explanation":"The source definition of density lists m as a defining input.","kind":"definitional"},{"descriptor_key":"graph_theory.n","explanation":"The source definition of density lists n as a defining input.","kind":"definitional"}],"dimension":null,"exactness":"approximate","expression":{"arguments":[{"kind":"variable","name":"G","sort":{"key":"graph_theory.finite_connected_simple_graph_value","parameters":[]}}],"kind":"application","symbol":"graph_theory.density"},"hypothesis_eligible":false,"key":"graph_theory.density","name":"Density","observation_key":"density","predictor_eligible":true,"provenance_references":["reference:theo-conjecture-web-fresh-graph-registry","source:theox-graph-template-normalization"],"role":"derived","scalar_constraints":[],"subject":{"kind":"variable","name":"G","sort":{"key":"graph_theory.finite_connected_simple_graph_value","parameters":[]}},"target_eligible":true,"unit":null,"value_kind":"real","value_sort":{"key":"core.real_value","parameters":[]}}
{"definition":"For vertices \\(u\\) and \\(v\\), the distance \\(d(u,v)\\) is the length of a shortest path joining them. The diameter \\(\\operatorname{diam}(G)\\) is \\(\\max\\{d(u,v):u,v\\in V(G)\\}\\). It is finite for connected graphs.","dependencies":[],"dimension":null,"exactness":"exact","expression":{"arguments":[{"kind":"variable","name":"G","sort":{"key":"graph_theory.finite_connected_simple_graph_value","parameters":[]}}],"kind":"application","symbol":"graph_theory.diameter"},"hypothesis_eligible":false,"key":"graph_theory.diameter","name":"Diameter","observation_key":"diameter","predictor_eligible":true,"provenance_references":["reference:theo-conjecture-web-fresh-graph-registry","source:theox-graph-template-normalization"],"role":"established","scalar_constraints":[],"subject":{"kind":"variable","name":"G","sort":{"key":"graph_theory.finite_connected_simple_graph_value","parameters":[]}},"target_eligible":true,"unit":null,"value_kind":"integer","value_sort":{"key":"core.integer_value","parameters":[]}}
{"definition":"The distinct degree count is \\(|\\{\\deg(v):v\\in V(G)\\}|\\). For example, a regular graph has distinct degree count 1, while a graph with vertices of degrees 1, 2, and 4 has distinct degree count 3.","dependencies":[],"dimension":null,"exactness":"exact","expression":{"arguments":[{"kind":"variable","name":"G","sort":{"key":"graph_theory.finite_connected_simple_graph_value","parameters":[]}}],"kind":"application","symbol":"graph_theory.distinct_degree_count"},"hypothesis_eligible":false,"key":"graph_theory.distinct_degree_count","name":"Distinct degree count","observation_key":"distinct_degree_count","predictor_eligible":true,"provenance_references":["reference:theo-conjecture-web-fresh-graph-registry","source:theox-graph-template-normalization"],"role":"established","scalar_constraints":[],"subject":{"kind":"variable","name":"G","sort":{"key":"graph_theory.finite_connected_simple_graph_value","parameters":[]}},"target_eligible":true,"unit":null,"value_kind":"integer","value_sort":{"key":"core.integer_value","parameters":[]}}
