{"definition":"In the domination game, two players, Dominator and Staller, alternately choose vertices of \\(G\\). A chosen vertex dominates itself and all of its neighbors. If \\(S\\) is the set of vertices chosen so far, then a move \\(v\\) is legal exactly when \\(N[v] \\setminus N[S] \\ne \\varnothing\\); in words, the move must dominate at least one vertex that was not already dominated. The game ends when \\(N[S]=V(G)\\), meaning every vertex is dominated by the chosen set. Dominator tries to minimize the total number of moves, Staller tries to maximize it, and the game domination number \\(\\gamma_{g}(G)\\) is this optimal total when Dominator moves first.","dependencies":[],"dimension":null,"exactness":"exact","expression":{"arguments":[{"kind":"variable","name":"G","sort":{"key":"graph_theory.finite_connected_simple_graph_value","parameters":[]}}],"kind":"application","symbol":"graph_theory.game_domination_number"},"hypothesis_eligible":false,"key":"graph_theory.game_domination_number","name":"Game domination number","observation_key":"game_domination_number","predictor_eligible":true,"provenance_references":["reference:theo-conjecture-web-fresh-graph-registry","source:theox-graph-template-normalization"],"role":"established","scalar_constraints":[],"subject":{"kind":"variable","name":"G","sort":{"key":"graph_theory.finite_connected_simple_graph_value","parameters":[]}},"target_eligible":true,"unit":null,"value_kind":"integer","value_sort":{"key":"core.integer_value","parameters":[]}}
{"definition":"In the isolation game, Dominator and Staller alternately choose vertices of \\(G\\). After the chosen set is \\(S\\), the closed neighborhood \\(N[S]\\) is treated as deleted, and the remaining graph is \\(G-N[S]\\). A move \\(v\\) is legal exactly when choosing \\(v\\) deletes at least one vertex that is still incident with an edge of the current remaining graph. After \\(v\\) is chosen, it is added to \\(S\\). The game ends when \\(G-N[S]\\) has no edges. Dominator tries to minimize the total number of moves, Staller tries to maximize it, and the game isolation number \\(\\iota_{g}(G)\\) is this optimal total when Dominator moves first.","dependencies":[],"dimension":null,"exactness":"exact","expression":{"arguments":[{"kind":"variable","name":"G","sort":{"key":"graph_theory.finite_connected_simple_graph_value","parameters":[]}}],"kind":"application","symbol":"graph_theory.game_isolation_number"},"hypothesis_eligible":false,"key":"graph_theory.game_isolation_number","name":"Game isolation number","observation_key":"game_isolation_number","predictor_eligible":true,"provenance_references":["reference:theo-conjecture-web-fresh-graph-registry","source:theox-graph-template-normalization"],"role":"established","scalar_constraints":[],"subject":{"kind":"variable","name":"G","sort":{"key":"graph_theory.finite_connected_simple_graph_value","parameters":[]}},"target_eligible":true,"unit":null,"value_kind":"integer","value_sort":{"key":"core.integer_value","parameters":[]}}
{"definition":"In the total domination game, Dominator and Staller alternately choose vertices of \\(G\\). A chosen vertex totally dominates its neighbors, but not itself. If \\(S\\) is the set of vertices chosen so far, then a move \\(v\\) is legal exactly when \\(N(v) \\setminus N(S) \\ne \\varnothing\\), where \\(N(S)\\) is the union of open neighborhoods of the vertices in \\(S\\); in words, the move must totally dominate at least one vertex that was not already totally dominated. The game ends when \\(N(S)=V(G)\\), meaning every vertex has a chosen neighbor. Dominator tries to minimize the total number of moves, Staller tries to maximize it, and the game total domination number \\(\\gamma_{tg}(G)\\) is this optimal total when Dominator moves first.","dependencies":[],"dimension":null,"exactness":"exact","expression":{"arguments":[{"kind":"variable","name":"G","sort":{"key":"graph_theory.finite_connected_simple_graph_value","parameters":[]}}],"kind":"application","symbol":"graph_theory.game_total_domination_number"},"hypothesis_eligible":false,"key":"graph_theory.game_total_domination_number","name":"Game total domination number","observation_key":"game_total_domination_number","predictor_eligible":true,"provenance_references":["reference:theo-conjecture-web-fresh-graph-registry","source:theox-graph-template-normalization"],"role":"established","scalar_constraints":[],"subject":{"kind":"variable","name":"G","sort":{"key":"graph_theory.finite_connected_simple_graph_value","parameters":[]}},"target_eligible":true,"unit":null,"value_kind":"integer","value_sort":{"key":"core.integer_value","parameters":[]}}
{"definition":"The total isolation game is the open-neighborhood version of the isolation game. Dominator and Staller alternately choose vertices of \\(G\\). A chosen vertex marks its neighbors, but not itself. If \\(S\\) is the chosen set, let \\(N(S)\\) be the union of open neighborhoods of vertices in \\(S\\), and put \\(U=V(G)\\setminus N(S)\\). The unresolved target consists of the chosen vertices still in \\(U\\), together with the vertices of \\(U\\setminus S\\) that have a neighbor in \\(U\\). A move \\(v\\notin S\\) is legal exactly when \\(N(v)\\) meets this target, meaning the move marks at least one unresolved vertex. The game ends when the target is empty; equivalently, every chosen vertex has a chosen neighbor, and the unmarked unchosen vertices induce an edgeless graph. Dominator tries to minimize the total number of moves, Staller tries to maximize it, and the game total isolation number \\(\\iota_{gt}(G)\\) is this optimal total when Dominator moves first.","dependencies":[],"dimension":null,"exactness":"exact","expression":{"arguments":[{"kind":"variable","name":"G","sort":{"key":"graph_theory.finite_connected_simple_graph_value","parameters":[]}}],"kind":"application","symbol":"graph_theory.game_total_isolation_number"},"hypothesis_eligible":false,"key":"graph_theory.game_total_isolation_number","name":"Game total isolation number","observation_key":"game_total_isolation_number","predictor_eligible":true,"provenance_references":["reference:theo-conjecture-web-fresh-graph-registry","source:theox-graph-template-normalization"],"role":"established","scalar_constraints":[],"subject":{"kind":"variable","name":"G","sort":{"key":"graph_theory.finite_connected_simple_graph_value","parameters":[]}},"target_eligible":true,"unit":null,"value_kind":"integer","value_sort":{"key":"core.integer_value","parameters":[]}}
