{"definition":"An independent dominating set is a set \\(S\\subseteq V(G)\\) that is both dominating and independent. Thus every vertex lies in \\(N[S]\\), and no two vertices of \\(S\\) are adjacent. The independent domination number \\(i(G)\\) is the minimum cardinality of such a set.","dependencies":[],"dimension":null,"exactness":"exact","expression":{"arguments":[{"kind":"variable","name":"G","sort":{"key":"graph_theory.finite_connected_simple_graph_value","parameters":[]}}],"kind":"application","symbol":"graph_theory.independent_domination_number"},"hypothesis_eligible":false,"key":"graph_theory.independent_domination_number","name":"Independent domination number","observation_key":"independent_domination_number","predictor_eligible":true,"provenance_references":["reference:theo-conjecture-web-fresh-graph-registry","source:theox-graph-template-normalization"],"role":"established","scalar_constraints":[],"subject":{"kind":"variable","name":"G","sort":{"key":"graph_theory.finite_connected_simple_graph_value","parameters":[]}},"target_eligible":true,"unit":null,"value_kind":"integer","value_sort":{"key":"core.integer_value","parameters":[]}}
{"definition":"The independent domination game is the domination game with an added independence rule. Dominator and Staller alternately choose vertices of \\(G\\). A move must newly dominate at least one vertex, so if \\(S\\) is the set chosen so far, \\(v\\) must satisfy \\(N[v] \\setminus N[S] \\ne \\varnothing\\). The chosen vertex also may not be adjacent to any previously chosen vertex, so the chosen set remains independent. The game ends when every vertex is dominated, equivalently when the chosen set is a maximal independent set. Dominator tries to minimize the total number of moves, Staller tries to maximize it, and the independent domination game number \\(I_{d}(G)\\) is this optimal total when Dominator moves first.","dependencies":[],"dimension":null,"exactness":"exact","expression":{"arguments":[{"kind":"variable","name":"G","sort":{"key":"graph_theory.finite_connected_simple_graph_value","parameters":[]}}],"kind":"application","symbol":"graph_theory.independent_game_domination_number"},"hypothesis_eligible":false,"key":"graph_theory.independent_game_domination_number","name":"Independent domination game number","observation_key":"independent_game_domination_number","predictor_eligible":true,"provenance_references":["reference:theo-conjecture-web-fresh-graph-registry","source:theox-graph-template-normalization"],"role":"established","scalar_constraints":[],"subject":{"kind":"variable","name":"G","sort":{"key":"graph_theory.finite_connected_simple_graph_value","parameters":[]}},"target_eligible":true,"unit":null,"value_kind":"integer","value_sort":{"key":"core.integer_value","parameters":[]}}
