{"definition":"An asteroidal triple is a set of three pairwise nonadjacent vertices such that, for any two of them, there is a path joining those two vertices that avoids the closed neighborhood of the third vertex. A graph \\(G\\) is AT-free if it has no asteroidal triple.","dependencies":[],"dimension":null,"exactness":"exact","expression":{"arguments":[{"kind":"variable","name":"G","sort":{"key":"graph_theory.finite_connected_simple_graph_value","parameters":[]}}],"kind":"relation","symbol":"graph_theory.is_at_free"},"hypothesis_eligible":true,"key":"graph_theory.is_at_free","name":"AT-free property","observation_key":"is_at_free","predictor_eligible":true,"provenance_references":["reference:theo-conjecture-web-fresh-graph-registry","source:theox-graph-template-normalization"],"role":"established","scalar_constraints":[],"subject":{"kind":"variable","name":"G","sort":{"key":"graph_theory.finite_connected_simple_graph_value","parameters":[]}},"target_eligible":true,"unit":null,"value_kind":"boolean","value_sort":{"key":"core.proposition","parameters":[]}}
{"definition":"A graph \\(G\\) is biconnected if it is connected and has no articulation vertex. Equivalently, for every vertex \\(v\\), the graph \\(G-v\\) remains connected whenever the deletion leaves at least two vertices.","dependencies":[],"dimension":null,"exactness":"exact","expression":{"arguments":[{"kind":"variable","name":"G","sort":{"key":"graph_theory.finite_connected_simple_graph_value","parameters":[]}}],"kind":"relation","symbol":"graph_theory.is_biconnected"},"hypothesis_eligible":true,"key":"graph_theory.is_biconnected","name":"Biconnected property","observation_key":"is_biconnected","predictor_eligible":true,"provenance_references":["reference:theo-conjecture-web-fresh-graph-registry","source:theox-graph-template-normalization"],"role":"established","scalar_constraints":[],"subject":{"kind":"variable","name":"G","sort":{"key":"graph_theory.finite_connected_simple_graph_value","parameters":[]}},"target_eligible":true,"unit":null,"value_kind":"boolean","value_sort":{"key":"core.proposition","parameters":[]}}
{"definition":"A graph \\(G\\) is bipartite if there is a partition \\(V(G)=A\\cup B\\) such that both \\(A\\) and \\(B\\) are independent sets. Equivalently, every edge has one endpoint in \\(A\\) and the other in \\(B\\).","dependencies":[],"dimension":null,"exactness":"exact","expression":{"arguments":[{"kind":"variable","name":"G","sort":{"key":"graph_theory.finite_connected_simple_graph_value","parameters":[]}}],"kind":"relation","symbol":"graph_theory.is_bipartite"},"hypothesis_eligible":true,"key":"graph_theory.is_bipartite","name":"Bipartite property","observation_key":"is_bipartite","predictor_eligible":true,"provenance_references":["reference:theo-conjecture-web-fresh-graph-registry","source:theox-graph-template-normalization"],"role":"established","scalar_constraints":[],"subject":{"kind":"variable","name":"G","sort":{"key":"graph_theory.finite_connected_simple_graph_value","parameters":[]}},"target_eligible":true,"unit":null,"value_kind":"boolean","value_sort":{"key":"core.proposition","parameters":[]}}
{"definition":"A bridge, also called a cut-edge, is an edge \\(e\\in E(G)\\) such that deleting \\(e\\) increases the number of connected components. A graph \\(G\\) is bridgeless if it has no such edge. Equivalently, every edge lies on at least one cycle in its connected component.","dependencies":[],"dimension":null,"exactness":"exact","expression":{"arguments":[{"kind":"variable","name":"G","sort":{"key":"graph_theory.finite_connected_simple_graph_value","parameters":[]}}],"kind":"relation","symbol":"graph_theory.is_bridgeless"},"hypothesis_eligible":true,"key":"graph_theory.is_bridgeless","name":"Bridgeless property","observation_key":"is_bridgeless","predictor_eligible":true,"provenance_references":["reference:theo-conjecture-web-fresh-graph-registry","source:theox-graph-template-normalization"],"role":"established","scalar_constraints":[],"subject":{"kind":"variable","name":"G","sort":{"key":"graph_theory.finite_connected_simple_graph_value","parameters":[]}},"target_eligible":true,"unit":null,"value_kind":"boolean","value_sort":{"key":"core.proposition","parameters":[]}}
{"definition":"A graph \\(G\\) is chordal if every cycle \\(C\\) with \\(|V(C)|\\ge 4\\) has a chord, that is, an edge joining two nonconsecutive vertices of the cycle. Equivalently, \\(G\\) has no induced cycle of length at least four.","dependencies":[],"dimension":null,"exactness":"exact","expression":{"arguments":[{"kind":"variable","name":"G","sort":{"key":"graph_theory.finite_connected_simple_graph_value","parameters":[]}}],"kind":"relation","symbol":"graph_theory.is_chordal"},"hypothesis_eligible":true,"key":"graph_theory.is_chordal","name":"Chordal property","observation_key":"is_chordal","predictor_eligible":true,"provenance_references":["reference:theo-conjecture-web-fresh-graph-registry","source:theox-graph-template-normalization"],"role":"established","scalar_constraints":[],"subject":{"kind":"variable","name":"G","sort":{"key":"graph_theory.finite_connected_simple_graph_value","parameters":[]}},"target_eligible":true,"unit":null,"value_kind":"boolean","value_sort":{"key":"core.proposition","parameters":[]}}
{"definition":"A claw is the star \\(K_{1,3}\\), with one center adjacent to three leaves and no edges among the leaves. A graph \\(G\\) is claw-free if no four vertices induce a subgraph isomorphic to this claw.","dependencies":[],"dimension":null,"exactness":"exact","expression":{"arguments":[{"kind":"variable","name":"G","sort":{"key":"graph_theory.finite_connected_simple_graph_value","parameters":[]}}],"kind":"relation","symbol":"graph_theory.is_claw_free"},"hypothesis_eligible":true,"key":"graph_theory.is_claw_free","name":"Claw-free property","observation_key":"is_claw_free","predictor_eligible":true,"provenance_references":["reference:theo-conjecture-web-fresh-graph-registry","source:theox-graph-template-normalization"],"role":"established","scalar_constraints":[],"subject":{"kind":"variable","name":"G","sort":{"key":"graph_theory.finite_connected_simple_graph_value","parameters":[]}},"target_eligible":true,"unit":null,"value_kind":"boolean","value_sort":{"key":"core.proposition","parameters":[]}}
{"definition":"A graph \\(G\\) is a cograph if it is \\(P_4\\)-free, meaning no four vertices induce a path with three edges. Equivalently, cographs are built from one-vertex graphs by repeated disjoint union and complement operations.","dependencies":[],"dimension":null,"exactness":"exact","expression":{"arguments":[{"kind":"variable","name":"G","sort":{"key":"graph_theory.finite_connected_simple_graph_value","parameters":[]}}],"kind":"relation","symbol":"graph_theory.is_cograph"},"hypothesis_eligible":true,"key":"graph_theory.is_cograph","name":"Cograph property","observation_key":"is_cograph","predictor_eligible":true,"provenance_references":["reference:theo-conjecture-web-fresh-graph-registry","source:theox-graph-template-normalization"],"role":"established","scalar_constraints":[],"subject":{"kind":"variable","name":"G","sort":{"key":"graph_theory.finite_connected_simple_graph_value","parameters":[]}},"target_eligible":true,"unit":null,"value_kind":"boolean","value_sort":{"key":"core.proposition","parameters":[]}}
{"definition":"A finite simple graph \\(G\\) is complete if every pair of distinct vertices is adjacent. Equivalently, \\(m(G)=n(G)(n(G)-1)/2\\). The empty graph and \\(K_1\\) satisfy this condition under the vacuous-pair convention.","dependencies":[{"descriptor_key":"graph_theory.n","explanation":"The source definition of is_complete lists n as a defining input.","kind":"definitional"},{"descriptor_key":"graph_theory.m","explanation":"The source definition of is_complete lists m as a defining input.","kind":"definitional"}],"dimension":null,"exactness":"exact","expression":{"arguments":[{"kind":"variable","name":"G","sort":{"key":"graph_theory.finite_connected_simple_graph_value","parameters":[]}}],"kind":"relation","symbol":"graph_theory.is_complete"},"hypothesis_eligible":true,"key":"graph_theory.is_complete","name":"Complete graph property","observation_key":"is_complete","predictor_eligible":true,"provenance_references":["reference:theo-conjecture-web-fresh-graph-registry","source:theox-graph-template-normalization"],"role":"derived","scalar_constraints":[],"subject":{"kind":"variable","name":"G","sort":{"key":"graph_theory.finite_connected_simple_graph_value","parameters":[]}},"target_eligible":true,"unit":null,"value_kind":"boolean","value_sort":{"key":"core.proposition","parameters":[]}}
