        "definition": "For each vertex \\(v\\), let \\(\\deg(v)\\) be its degree. The augmented Zagreb index \\(\\operatorname{AZI}(G)\\) is obtained by summing the edge contribution \\(\\left(\\frac{\\deg(u)\\deg(v)}{\\deg(u)+\\deg(v)-2}\\right)^3\\) over all edges \\(uv\\in E(G)\\). The value depends only on the degrees of adjacent vertex pairs.",
