        "definition": "The average degree of \\(G\\) is \\((1/n(G))\\sum_{v\\in V(G)}\\deg(v)\\), the arithmetic mean of all vertex degrees. Since each edge contributes 1 to the degree of each endpoint, this is equal to \\(2m(G)/n(G)\\) for nonempty graphs.",
