        "definition": "In the graph burning process, all vertices start unburned. In each round, one unburned vertex may be chosen as a new source of fire, and simultaneously fire spreads from vertices burned in earlier rounds to their unburned neighbors. Once a vertex is burned it stays burned. The burning number \\(b(G)\\) is the minimum number of rounds needed until every vertex is burned.",
