        "definition": "A connected dominating set is a dominating set \\(S\\subseteq V(G)\\) such that the induced subgraph \\(G[S]\\) is connected. The connected domination number \\(\\gamma_{c}(G)\\) is the minimum cardinality of a connected dominating set. This requires \\(S\\) to dominate the whole graph and also be connected internally.",
