        "definition": "The connected domination game is the domination game with an added connectivity rule. Dominator and Staller alternately choose vertices of \\(G\\). A move must newly dominate at least one vertex, so if \\(S\\) is the set chosen so far, \\(v\\) must satisfy \\(N[v] \\setminus N[S] \\ne \\varnothing\\). In addition, after the first move, each new chosen vertex must be adjacent to at least one previously chosen vertex. Thus the chosen vertices always induce a connected subgraph. The game ends when \\(N[S]=V(G)\\), meaning every vertex is dominated. Dominator tries to minimize the total number of moves, Staller tries to maximize it, and the Staller-start connected game domination number \\(\\gamma'_{cg}(G)\\) is this optimal total when Staller moves first.",
