          "parameters": []
        },
        "role": "function"
      },
      {
        "body_sort": null,
        "bound_sorts": [],
        "definition": "For each edge \\(e\\in E(G)\\), form \\(G-e\\) by deleting that edge while keeping all vertices. The zero forcing noncritical edge count is the number of edges satisfying \\(Z(G-e)=Z(G)\\). These are the edges whose deletion does not change the zero forcing number.",
        "input_sorts": [
          {
            "key": "graph_theory.finite_connected_simple_graph_value",
