        "role": "function"
      },
      {
        "body_sort": null,
        "bound_sorts": [],
        "definition": "The zero forcing ratio is Z(G)/n(G), where Z(G) is the zero forcing number and n(G) is the number of vertices. It measures the fraction of vertices that must be initially colored in a smallest zero forcing set. It is undefined for the empty graph because n(G)=0.",
        "input_sorts": [
          {
