        "role": "predicate"
      },
      {
        "body_sort": null,
        "bound_sorts": [],
        "definition": "In deterministic Zombies and Survivor, \\(k\\) zombies are placed on vertices of \\(G\\), with multiple zombies allowed to occupy the same vertex. After seeing those choices, one survivor chooses a starting vertex. Zombies move first, and then the players alternate turns. On a zombie turn, every zombie must move to an adjacent vertex that is one step closer to the survivor, equivalently to a neighbor on a shortest path to the survivor. If more than one such neighbor is available, the zombie team may choose among them as part of its strategy. On a survivor turn, the survivor may either stay on the current vertex or move to an adjacent vertex. The zombies win if, after any move, at least one zombie occupies the survivor's vertex. The zombie number \\(z(G)\\) is the minimum \\(k\\) for which the zombies have a strategy that guarantees eventual capture against every legal survivor strategy. For disconnected inputs, this registry returns the sum of the zombie numbers of the connected components.",
